  "question": {
    "text": "If the complex numbers <math><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sin</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cos</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi></math> and <math><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cos</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>i</mi><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sin</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></math> are conjugate of each other, then the number of values of <math><mi>x</mi></math> in the interval <math><mfenced open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0,2</mn><mi>π</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is equal to (where, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math>)",
